---
import SiteLayout from '@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
---

<SiteLayout
  title={`Career Journey · ${site.name}`}
  description="Explore Eshan Naik's career experience and education."
>
  <section class="page-hero container">
    <p class="eyebrow">CAREER &amp; EDUCATION</p>
    <h1>
      A journey of
      <br />
      <em>continuous growth.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="hero-intro">
      From building enterprise data systems in manufacturing and transportation
      to designing cloud-based analytical platforms in financial services, my
      career has been shaped by diverse challenges and continuous learning.
      Alongside professional experience, my academic journey has expanded my
      perspective across data science, machine learning and business analytics.
      Together, these experiences have shaped how I approach technology, solve
      business problems and take on greater ownership.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="section container journey-section">
    <h2>Career &amp; education</h2>
    <p class="journey-intro">
      A few milestones that have shaped my growth across technology and
      analytics.
    </p>
    <div
      class="journey-timeline"
      role="list"
      aria-label="Career and education timeline"
    >
      <div class="journey-timeline-track" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="journey-timeline-progress"></div>
      </div>
      <div
        class="journey-event journey-overlap-event"
        role="listitem"
        aria-label="ISB study overlapped with Sigmoid and Equifax roles"
      >
        <article class="journey-card journey-isb-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">EDUCATION · PART-TIME ALONGSIDE WORK</p>
          <h3>Indian School of Business</h3>
          <p class="journey-card-date">July 2025 - October 2026</p>
          <p>
            Advanced Management Programme in
            <strong>Business Analytics and AI (AMPBA)</strong>
          </p>
          <p class="journey-overlap-note">
            Completed <strong>while working</strong>, first at
            <strong>Sigmoid</strong> and then at <strong>Equifax</strong>.
          </p>
          <details class="journey-highlights">
            <summary>View capstone project</summary>
            <section class="journey-capstone" aria-labelledby="capstone-title">
              <p class="eyebrow">CAPSTONE PROJECT</p>
              <h4 id="capstone-title">
                Thermal Imaging-Based Computer Vision for Ladle Monitoring
              </h4>
              <p class="journey-capstone-program">
                ISB · Advanced Management Programme in Business Analytics and AI
              </p>
              <p>
                Explored the application of
                <strong>computer vision and machine intelligence</strong> to
                <strong>industrial ladle monitoring</strong> using
                <strong>thermal imaging</strong>.
              </p>
              <p>
                The project connected
                <strong>image-based intelligence</strong> with
                <strong>practical manufacturing requirements</strong>, applying
                computer vision and machine learning concepts to an industrial
                monitoring use case.
              </p>
              <p class="journey-capstone-label">Focus areas</p>
              <ul class="journey-capstone-focus">
                <li>Thermal imaging and computer vision</li>
                <li>Machine intelligence for industrial applications</li>
                <li>Image-based analysis and monitoring</li>
                <li>Applying AI techniques to manufacturing use cases</li>
              </ul>
            </section>
          </details>
        </article>
        <div class="journey-marker">
          <span>Jul 2025 - Oct 2026</span>
        </div>
        <div class="journey-overlap-career">
          <article class="journey-card journey-overlap-equifax">
            <p class="eyebrow">EXPERIENCE</p>
            <h3>Equifax</h3>
            <p class="journey-card-role">
              Data Engineer 2 · Analytical Data Mart
            </p>
            <p class="journey-card-date">June 2026 - Present</p>
            <p>
              Leading implementation of a large-scale Azure Databricks
              analytical data platform for credit analytics, with reusable
              pipelines and business-focused data marts.
            </p>
            <details class="journey-highlights">
              <summary>View Equifax highlights</summary>
              <section class="journey-highlight-panel">
                <p class="eyebrow">PLATFORM ENGINEERING</p>
                <h4>Enterprise credit analytics data platform</h4>
                <p class="journey-highlight-program">
                  Azure Databricks · PySpark · Delta Lake · 20M+ records daily
                </p>

                <p class="journey-highlight-section-title">
                  Architecture &amp; platform scale
                </p>
                <ul class="journey-highlight-list">
                  <li>
                    Led technical implementation of a large-scale analytical
                    data platform processing approximately
                    <strong>20 million records daily</strong> across
                    <strong>150 source tables</strong>, 60+ dimensions and 10
                    fact tables.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Contributed to the architecture of
                    <strong>10 business data marts</strong> supporting more than
                    <strong>2,000 credit KPIs</strong> through Databricks Metric
                    Views.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Designed a reusable,
                    <strong>metadata-driven PySpark framework</strong> using
                    configuration and control tables to standardize pipeline
                    execution across multiple data domains.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Established <strong>modular processing patterns</strong> for
                    pre-execution validation, business transformations, schema
                    alignment, data quality checks and controlled writes.
                  </li>
                </ul>

                <p class="journey-highlight-section-title">
                  Data quality, reliability &amp; observability
                </p>
                <ul class="journey-highlight-list">
                  <li>
                    Implemented{' '}
                    <strong>
                      centralized logging, data quality metrics, record-level
                      quarantine and resilient retry handling
                    </strong>{' '}
                    to improve pipeline reliability and operational visibility.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Worked on schema alignment and
                    <strong>schema drift handling</strong> to identify
                    unexpected structural changes and prevent invalid data from
                    progressing through downstream workflows.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Designed reusable{' '}
                    <strong>validation and monitoring patterns</strong>,
                    including centralized quality reporting and SLA-oriented
                    alerting.
                  </li>
                </ul>

                <p class="journey-highlight-section-title">
                  Governance &amp; data security
                </p>
                <ul class="journey-highlight-list">
                  <li>
                    Implemented governance practices using
                    <strong>Unity Catalog</strong>, role-based access control
                    (RBAC) and <strong>governed data access</strong> patterns.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Worked on{' '}
                    <strong>
                      attribute-based access control (ABAC), governed tags and
                      data masking
                    </strong>{' '}
                    to strengthen access management for sensitive credit
                    datasets.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Incorporated{' '}
                    <strong>data protection and controlled access</strong>{' '}
                    considerations into the platform architecture and deployment
                    approach.
                  </li>
                </ul>

                <p class="journey-highlight-section-title">
                  Performance &amp; optimization
                </p>
                <ul class="journey-highlight-list">
                  <li>
                    Applied Databricks performance practices including
                    <strong>Liquid Clustering</strong>, Delta Lake optimization
                    and <strong>efficient Spark processing</strong> strategies.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Leveraged{' '}
                    <strong>Serverless SQL and Databricks Metric Views</strong>{' '}
                    to support analytical consumption and reusable KPI
                    definitions.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Considered{' '}
                    <strong>scalability and execution efficiency</strong>
                    across high-volume processing and downstream analytical
                    workloads.
                  </li>
                </ul>

                <p class="journey-highlight-section-title">
                  CI/CD &amp; engineering practices
                </p>
                <ul class="journey-highlight-list">
                  <li>
                    Worked on deployment automation using
                    <strong>Databricks Asset Bundles (DAB)</strong> and Azure
                    DevOps, structuring resources and configurations for
                    <strong>controlled environment deployments</strong>.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Contributed to <strong>CI/CD workflows</strong> covering
                    code quality, automated testing, validation and deployment
                    across development, QA and production environments.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Worked with{' '}
                    <strong>
                      Azure Repos, feature branching and pull requests
                    </strong>
                    , pipeline configuration and release coordination to improve
                    engineering consistency.
                  </li>
                </ul>

                <p class="journey-highlight-section-title">
                  Technical delivery &amp; team leadership
                </p>
                <ul class="journey-highlight-list">
                  <li>
                    Owned technical delivery across{' '}
                    <strong>
                      phases 2–4 for a four-member engineering team
                    </strong>
                    , translating high-level design into implementation tasks
                    and delivery milestones.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Contributed to{' '}
                    <strong>
                      HLDs, technical documentation and architecture decisions
                    </strong>
                    , sprint planning and Jira work-item decomposition.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <strong>Mentored three developers</strong> on Databricks,
                    PySpark, implementation practices and platform architecture.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Coordinated engineering activities across development,
                    testing and deployment, helping drive
                    <strong>
                      delivery from technical design through production
                      readiness
                    </strong>
                    .
                  </li>
                </ul>

                <p class="journey-highlight-section-title">Technology stack</p>
                <ul class="journey-highlight-focus">
                  <li>Azure Databricks &amp; PySpark</li>
                  <li>Delta Lake &amp; Metric Views</li>
                  <li>Unity Catalog &amp; ABAC</li>
                  <li>RBAC &amp; Data Masking</li>
                  <li>Databricks Asset Bundles</li>
                  <li>Azure DevOps &amp; CI/CD</li>
                  <li>SQL &amp; Serverless SQL</li>
                  <li>Jira &amp; Agile Delivery</li>
                  <li>Data Quality &amp; Observability</li>
                </ul>
              </section>
            </details>
          </article>
          <article class="journey-card journey-overlap-sigmoid">
            <p class="eyebrow">EXPERIENCE</p>
            <h3>Sigmoid</h3>
            <p class="journey-card-role">
              Data Engineer · NAC Supply Reporting
            </p>
            <p class="journey-card-date">June 2025 - June 2026</p>
            <p>
              Modernized a legacy financial reporting platform, migrating
              <strong>50+ pipelines</strong> to Azure and improving stability by
              approximately <strong>40%</strong>.
            </p>
            <details class="journey-highlights">
              <summary>View Sigmoid highlights</summary>
              <section class="journey-highlight-panel">
                <p class="eyebrow">DATA PLATFORM MODERNIZATION</p>
                <h4>Financial reporting on Azure</h4>
                <p class="journey-highlight-program">
                  NAC Supply Reporting · Data engineering
                </p>
                <p>
                  Modernized a legacy reporting platform, moving financial data
                  workflows from SFTP and SSIS to the Azure ecosystem.
                </p>
                <p class="journey-highlight-section-title">
                  Engineering highlights
                </p>
                <ul class="journey-highlight-list">
                  <li>
                    Migrated <strong>more than 50 SFTP/SSIS pipelines</strong>
                    to Azure Data Lake, Data Factory and Databricks.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Designed Delta Lake storage and ingestion workflows
                    processing approximately{' '}
                    <strong>2 million records daily across 75+ tables</strong>.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Optimized <strong>Spark transformations</strong> and
                    implemented{' '}
                    <strong>incremental, idempotent processing</strong>
                    using Delta MERGE.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Improved pipeline stability and
                    <strong>reduced batch failures by approximately 40%</strong>
                    .
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Implemented{' '}
                    <strong>
                      Unity Catalog governance and role-based access controls
                    </strong>{' '}
                    across 10+ user groups.
                  </li>
                </ul>
                <p class="journey-highlight-section-title">Focus areas</p>
                <ul class="journey-highlight-focus">
                  <li>Azure Data Lake &amp; Data Factory</li>
                  <li>Databricks &amp; Delta Lake</li>
                  <li>Incremental, idempotent processing</li>
                  <li>Unity Catalog &amp; RBAC</li>
                </ul>
              </section>
            </details>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>

      <article class="journey-event journey-event-right" role="listitem">
        <div aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="journey-marker">
          <span>Jul 2022 - Jun 2025</span>
        </div>
        <div class="journey-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">EXPERIENCE</p>
          <h3>Daimler Trucks</h3>
          <p class="journey-card-role">Consultant · TransIT and DSFM</p>
          <p class="journey-card-date">July 2022 - June 2025</p>
          <p>
            My early professional experience was rooted in manufacturing and
            transportation analytics, working with enterprise-scale data systems
            and operational reporting.
          </p>
          <details class="journey-highlights">
            <summary>View Daimler highlights</summary>
            <section class="journey-highlight-panel">
              <p class="eyebrow">MANUFACTURING &amp; TRANSPORT ANALYTICS</p>
              <h4>TransIT and DSFM</h4>
              <p class="journey-highlight-program">
                Enterprise data platforms · Operational reporting
              </p>
              <section class="journey-highlight-group">
                <h4>
                  TransIT <span>January 2024 - June 2025</span>
                </h4>
                <ul>
                  <li>
                    Architected and maintained a
                    <strong>distributed on-premise data platform</strong> with
                    <strong>
                      85+ production pipelines and 100+ SAP integrations
                    </strong>
                    .
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Designed dimensional data models supporting transportation
                    analytics across <strong>5,000+ suppliers</strong> and
                    multiple European plants.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Owned ETL orchestration and monitoring, sustaining a
                    <strong>99.8% SLA</strong>.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Built KPI data architecture powering
                    <strong>30+ Tableau dashboards</strong> for
                    <strong>operational and shop-floor analytics</strong>.
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </section>
              <section class="journey-highlight-group">
                <h4>
                  DSFM <span>July 2022 - December 2023</span>
                </h4>
                <ul>
                  <li>
                    Independently designed and deployed
                    <strong>
                      10+ plant-specific analytics boards covering 100+ KPIs
                    </strong>
                    .
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Built{' '}
                    <strong>real-time and batch ingestion pipelines</strong>
                    integrating Talend, Kafka, Theobald and SQL Server.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Supported <strong>60+ monitored pipelines</strong>,
                    achieving <strong>99.5% operational reliability</strong>.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Implemented <strong>observability and logging</strong> to
                    improve production monitoring and incident response.
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </section>
              <p class="journey-highlight-section-title">Focus areas</p>
              <ul class="journey-highlight-focus">
                <li>Enterprise data architecture</li>
                <li>SAP integrations &amp; ETL orchestration</li>
                <li>Transportation and plant analytics</li>
                <li>Observability &amp; reliability</li>
              </ul>
            </section>
          </details>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="journey-event journey-event-left" role="listitem">
        <div class="journey-card journey-pes-card">
          <div class="journey-pes-header">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">EDUCATION</p>
              <h3>PES University</h3>
              <p class="journey-pes-degree">B.Tech, Computer Science</p>
              <p class="journey-card-date">August 2018 - June 2022</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="journey-pes-details">
            <div>
              <p class="journey-pes-label">Specialization</p>
              <p class="journey-pes-value">
                Data Science &amp; Machine Learning
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="journey-pes-label">Academic record</p>
              <p class="journey-pes-score">7/8</p>
              <p class="journey-pes-caption">Semesters with distinction</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="journey-marker">
          <span>Aug 2018 - Jun 2022</span>
        </div>
        <div aria-hidden="true"></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
